/// Real production data, frozen: the `grid_membership_index` RPC payload for nba (trimmed to
/// its 14 most-represented franchises so the fixture stays small), plus the answers
/// `tools/ingest/grid.py` produces for a sample of cells drawn from those franchises.
///
/// This is the drift guard between the two generators. `GridLocalGenerator` is a *second*
/// implementation of grid.py's cell rules, and the reason a client-side generator was deferred
/// for so long is that two implementations diverge silently. These expectations were computed by
/// running grid.py's own `_build_cell` against the live `player_seasons` catalog — not by
/// writing down what the Swift produced — so a change to either side that breaks agreement fails
/// `GridCrossCheckTests`.
///
/// Trimming to a subset of teams is exact, not an approximation: a cell's answers depend only on
/// the memberships of the teams on its axes, and every membership of a kept team is kept.
///
/// NBA on purpose — it has no `nfl_rosters` roster widening, so grid.py's answers are
/// the graded pool exactly, and the comparison carries no asterisk. (NFL daily boards widen
/// validity with ~69k roster-only memberships that `player_seasons` doesn't carry; an NFL
/// practice cell is therefore narrower than its daily counterpart, never wider.)
///
/// Regenerate with `scratchpad/build_crosscheck.py` if the catalog changes shape.
